  "final_answer": "I now have comprehensive information about both Coursera for Business and Coursera for Teams. Let me compile the final summary.\n\n## Summary of Coursera for Business and Coursera for Teams Advantages\n\n### **Coursera for Business (Enterprise)**\nCoursera for Business is positioned as \"the expert-powered learning platform that drives business growth,\" designed for organizations of all sizes. Its key advantages include:\n\n1. **Proven Performance Metrics:**\n   - **25% increase** in employee productivity\n   - **+38% higher** employee retention\n   - **97% employee engagement** in non-mandatory training\n\n2. **Premium Content Quality:**\n   - High-quality e-learning content from **350+ leading companies and universities**\n   - Courses from **20+ top global business schools**\n   - Industry-recognized credentials\n\n3. **Extensive Catalog:**\n   - **10,600+ courses**\n   - **1,400+ specializations**\n   - **165+ Professional Certificates**\n\n4. **Diverse Learning Formats:**\n   - Video clips, Professional Certificates, and Specializations tailored to learner preferences\n   - **Skill Tracks** for role-specific learning paths (Data Skills Track, IT Skills Track, GenAI Skills Track)\n\n5. **AI-Powered Personalization:**\n   - AI tools that deliver tailored learning paths\n   - Customizable training programs for organizations\n\n---\n\n### **Coursera for Teams**\nCoursera for Teams is aimed at smaller organizations (2 to 499 employees) and helps them upskill their workforce to grow their business. Its key advantages include:\n\n1. **Targeted for Growing Teams:**\n   - Designed for **2 to 499 employees**\n   - Pricing at **$399/year per user** (with bulk discounts at 25+ licenses)\n   - Trusted by **3,700+ teams worldwide**\n\n2. **World-Class Content Partners:**\n   - **325+ leading university and industry partners**, including Stanford, Duke, Google, University of Michigan, IBM, Imperial College London, and UPenn\n\n3. **Massive Learning Library:**\n   - **12,000+ courses**\n   - **140+ certificates**\n   - **1,500+ hands-on labs**\n   - **200,000+ clips**\n\n4. **Globally Recognized Credentials:**\n   - Professional Certificates from top institutions\n   - Helps build high-performing teams with courses in business, data, and tech from Google, University of Michigan, IBM, etc.\n\n5. **AI-Powered Customization:**\n   - Personalized AI guidance to accelerate skill growth\n   - Multilingual, role-specific learning paths\n\n6. **In-Demand Skill Topics:**\n   - Data Analysis, Generative AI, Machine Learning, Python Programming, Cloud Computing, Project Management\n\n7. **Tackles Key Workforce Challenges:**\n   - 72% of US CEOs prioritize generative AI as a top investment\n   - 60% of employees need retraining by 2026 to stay competitive\n   - 70%+ of employees using GenAI expect it to boost skills, creativity, and work quality\n\n8. **Employee Engagement & Retention:**\n   - Keep your best people longer and help them grow\n   - Increase positive business impact through continuous learning\n\n9. **Flexible Billing & Policies:**\n   - 14-day refund policy\n   - License transfers (up to 10% per billing cycle)\n   - Add licenses anytime with prorated pricing\n   - Multiple payment options: credit card, PayPal, or invoice\n\n---\n\n### **Key Difference Between the Two:**\n- **Coursera for Business** is geared toward larger enterprises with unlimited content access and is sold through sales conversations.\n- **Coursera for Teams** is a self-serve product targeted at smaller teams (2-499 employees) with transparent pricing ($399/user/year) and the full enterprise content library.",
